DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19800218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19800219
SUMMARY:1980 Canadian federal election (Canada)
DESCRIPTION:The 1980 Canadian federal election was held on February 18\, 19
 80\, to elect members of the House of Commons of Canada of the 32nd Parlia
 ment of Canada. It was called when the budget of the minority Progressive 
 Conservative government led by Prime Minister Joe Clark was defeated in th
 e Commons.\n\nElection: Canada\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980
 _Canadian_federal_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian
  Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Election
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_Canadian_federal_election
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:56f65a8738efa80b@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19800218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19800219
SUMMARY:1980 Saint Kitts and Nevis general election
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Saint Kitts and Nevis on 18 Febr
 uary 1980. Although the Saint Kitts and Nevis Labour Party won a plurality
  of the elected seats\, the People's Action Movement (PAM) were able to fo
 rm a coalition government with the Nevis Reformation Party which held a on
 e-seat majority. PAM leader Kennedy Simmonds became Premier.\n\nElection: 
 Saint Kitts and Nevis\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_Saint_Ki
 tts_and_Nevis_general_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitru
 vian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Election
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_Saint_Kitts_and_Nevis_general_electi
 on
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:132b382fb367d607@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19800225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19800226
SUMMARY:Coup: 1980 Surinamese coup d'état
DESCRIPTION:The 1980 Surinamese coup d'état\, usually referred to as the S
 ergeants' Coup\, was a military coup in Suriname which occurred on 25 Febr
 uary 1980\, when a group of 16 sergeants of the Surinamese Armed Forces (S
 KM) led by Dési Bouterse overthrew the government of Prime Minister Henck
  Arron with a violent coup d'état.\n\nCoup: Suriname\nSource: https://en.
 wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_Surinamese_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat\nText: Wikipedia (CC
  BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Coup
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_Surinamese_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
