DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19800424
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19800425
SUMMARY:1980 Antiguan general election (Antigua and Barbuda)
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Antigua and Barbuda on 24 April 
 1980. They were won by the governing Antigua Labour Party. ALP leader Vere
  Bird was re-elected as Prime Minister of Antigua and Barbuda. Voter turno
 ut was 77.1%.\n\nElection: Antigua and Barbuda\nSource: https://en.wikiped
 ia.org/wiki/1980_Antiguan_general_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)
 \, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
