SUMMARY:Terrorist attack: Bologna massacre (Italy)
DESCRIPTION:The Bologna massacre was a terrorist bombing of the Bologna Cen
 trale railway station in Bologna\, Italy\, on the morning of 2 August 1980
 \, which killed 85 people and wounded over 200. Several members of the neo
 -fascist terrorist organization Nuclei Armati Rivoluzionari were sentenced
  for the bombing\, although the group denied involvement.\n\nCrisis: Italy
 \nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bologna_massacre\nText: Wikipedia 
 (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Crisis
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bologna_massacre
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
