DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19800913
SUMMARY:1980 Turkish presidential election (Turkey)
DESCRIPTION:The 1980 Turkish presidential election refers to the unsuccessf
 ul election process to choose the country's seventh president\, to succeed
  Fahri Korutürk. The first round of the election was held on 12 March 198
 0. There were 115 unsuccessful rounds until 12 September 1980. The electio
 n ended with a coup d'état on that date.\n\nElection: Turkey\nSource: htt
 ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1980_Turkish_presidential_election\nText: Wikip
 edia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
