DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19801124
SUMMARY:Earthquake: 1980 Irpinia earthquake (Italy)
DESCRIPTION:The 1980 Irpinia earthquake took place in Italy on 23 November 
 1980\, with a moment magnitude of 6.9 and a maximum Mercalli intensity of 
 X (Extreme). It left at least 2\,483 people dead\, at least 7\,700 injured
 \, and 250\,000 homeless.\n\nCrisis: Italy\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.o
 rg/wiki/1980_Irpinia_earthquake\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitr
 uvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
