DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Bulgaria on 7 June 1981. T
 he Fatherland Front\, dominated by the Bulgarian Communist Party\, was the
  only organisation to contest the election\; all candidate lists had to be
  approved by the Front. The Front nominated one candidate for each constit
 uency.\n\nElection: Bulgaria\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1981_B
 ulgarian_parliamentary_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitr
