SUMMARY:1981 Israeli legislative election
DESCRIPTION:Legislative elections were held in Israel on 30 June 1981 to el
 ect the 120 members of the Knesset. The ruling Likud won one more seat tha
 n the opposition Alignment\, in line with many polls which had predicted a
  tight race. Voter turnout was 78.5%\, with Likud receiving around ten tho
 usand more than the Alignment.\n\nElection: Israel\nSource: https://en.wik
 ipedia.org/wiki/1981_Israeli_legislative_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-
