DESCRIPTION:The United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS)\, 
 also called the Law of the Sea Convention or the Law of the Sea Treaty\, i
 s an international treaty that establishes a legal framework for all marin
 e and maritime activities. As of October 2024\, 169 sovereign states and t
 he European Union are parties to the convention.\n\nTreaty: International\
