SUMMARY:1983 Austrian legislative election
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Austria on 24 April 1983. 
 The result saw the Socialist Party win 90 of 183 seats\, enough to secure 
 them a fifth term in government\, albeit without the absolute majority the
  party had held since 1971. This prompted Bruno Kreisky to stand down as S
 PÖ leader and Chancellor in favour of Fred Sinowatz.\n\nElection: Austria
 \nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1983_Austrian_legislative_election
