DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19830724
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19830725
SUMMARY:Black July (Sri Lanka)
DESCRIPTION:Black July was an anti-Tamil pogrom that occurred in Sri Lanka 
 during July 1983. The pogrom was premeditated\, and was finally triggered 
 by a deadly ambush on a Sri Lankan Army patrol by the Liberation Tigers of
  Tamil Eelam (LTTE) on 23 July 1983\, which killed 13 soldiers.\n\nProtest
 : Sri Lanka\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_July\nText: Wikip
 edia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Protest
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_July
