DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19831002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19831003
SUMMARY:1983 Labour Party leadership election (UK) (United Kingdom)
DESCRIPTION:The 1983 Labour Party leadership election was an election in th
 e United Kingdom for the leadership of the Labour Party. It occurred when 
 Michael Foot resigned as Leader after the party won only 209 seats at the 
 1983 general election\, a loss of 60 seats from its performance at the pre
 vious election four years earlier.\n\nParty contest: United Kingdom\nSourc
 e: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1983_Labour_Party_leadership_election_(UK
 )\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev)
