DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19831024
SUMMARY:Terrorist attack: 1983 Beirut barracks bombings (Lebanon)
DESCRIPTION:On October 23\, 1983\, two truck bombs were detonated at buildi
 ngs in Beirut\, Lebanon\, housing American and French service members of t
 he Multinational Force in Lebanon (MNF)\, a military peacekeeping operatio
 n during the Lebanese Civil War. The attack killed 307 people: 241 U.S. an
 d 58 French military personnel\, six civilians and both the attackers.\n\n
 Crisis: Lebanon\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1983_Beirut_barrack
 s_bombings\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.p
 ages.dev).
