DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19831024
SUMMARY:1983 Swiss federal election (Switzerland)
DESCRIPTION:Federal elections were held in Switzerland on 23 October 1983. 
 The Free Democratic Party emerged as the largest party in the National Cou
 ncil\, winning 54 of the 200 seats. It was the first time the Social Democ
 ratic Party had not received the most votes in a federal election since 19
 25.\n\nElection: Switzerland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1983_S
 wiss_federal_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Mana
 ger (jdpi.pages.dev).
