SUMMARY:1983 Jamaican general election
DESCRIPTION:Early general elections were held in Jamaica on 15 December 198
 3. The elections were effectively ended as a contest when the main opposit
 ion party\, the People's National Party\, boycotted the election to protes
 t the refusal of the ruling Jamaican Labour Party to update the electoral 
 roll amid allegations of voter fraud.\n\nElection: Jamaica\nSource: https:
 //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1983_Jamaican_general_election\nText: Wikipedia (C
 C BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
