DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19831228
SUMMARY:Tunisian bread riots
DESCRIPTION:The Tunisian bread riots were a series of violent demonstration
 s in Tunisia that occurred from December 1983 to January 1984\, triggered 
 by a rise in the price of bread due to an IMF-imposed austerity program. P
 resident Habib Bourguiba declared a state of emergency and the riots were 
 put down by force. Over 100 rioters died.\n\nProtest: Tunisia\nSource: htt
 ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunisian_bread_riots\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA
  4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
