SUMMARY:1984 Danish general election (Denmark)
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Denmark on 10 January 1984\, aft
 er the opposition voted against the centre-right four-party government's s
 tate budget bill. Although the Social Democratic Party remained the larges
 t in the Folketing with 56 of the 179 seats\, the Conservative People's Pa
 rty achieved its best-ever result\, gaining 16 seats.\n\nElection: Denmark
