SUMMARY:Sony Corp. of America v. Universal City Studios\, Inc. (United Stat
 es)
DESCRIPTION:Sony Corp. of America v. Universal City Studios\, Inc.\, 464 U.
 S. 417 (1984)\, also known as the "Betamax case"\, is a decision by the Su
 preme Court of the United States which ruled that the making of individual
  copies of complete television shows for purposes of time shifting does no
 t constitute copyright infringement\, but can instead be defended as fair 
 use.\n\nCourt ruling: United States\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki
 /Sony_Corp._of_America_v._Universal_City_Studios\,_Inc.\nText: Wikipedia (
