DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19841012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19841013
SUMMARY:Terrorist attack: Brighton hotel bombing (United Kingdom)
DESCRIPTION:On 12 October 1984 the Provisional Irish Republican Army (IRA) 
 attempted to assassinate members of the British government\, including the
  prime minister\, Margaret Thatcher\, at the Grand Hotel in Brighton\, Eng
 land. Five people were killed\, including the Conservative MP Sir Anthony 
 Berry\; more than thirty people were injured. Thatcher was uninjured.\n\nC
 risis: United Kingdom\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brighton_hote
 l_bombing\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pa
 ges.dev).
CATEGORIES:Crisis
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brighton_hotel_bombing
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
