UID:22387e10bb56a804@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19841019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19841020
SUMMARY:Assassination of Jerzy Popiełuszko (Poland)
DESCRIPTION:On the night of 19 October 1984\, 37-year-old Polish Catholic p
 riest Jerzy Popiełuszko was attacked\, kidnapped\, and killed by three ag
 ents of the Polish Security Service\, the communist counterintelligence ag
 ency in Polish People's Republic\, who were disguised as traffic police.\n
 \nAssassination: Poland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassinati
 on_of_Jerzy_Popie%C5%82uszko\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvi
 an Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Assassination
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Jerzy_Popie%C5%82uszko
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:75783cca7ddc194e@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19841031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19841101
SUMMARY:Assassination of Indira Gandhi (India)
DESCRIPTION:Indira Gandhi\, the Indian prime minister\, was assassinated at
  9:30 am on 31 October 1984 at her residence in Safdarjung Road\, New Delh
 i by her two bodyguards\, Satwant Singh and Beant Singh. This was after th
 e Indian Armed Forces carried out Operation Blue Star between 1 and 8 June
  1984 on Gandhi's orders.\n\nAssassination: India\nSource: https://en.wiki
 pedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Indira_Gandhi\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4
 .0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Assassination
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Indira_Gandhi
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ca54fb66a31d84f8@jdpi.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19841031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19841101
SUMMARY:1984 anti-Sikh riots (India)
DESCRIPTION:The 1984 anti-Sikh riots\, also known as the 1984 Sikh massacre
 \, were a series of organised pogroms against Sikhs in India following the
  assassination of Indira Gandhi by her Sikh bodyguards. Government estimat
 es were that about 2\,800 Sikhs were killed in Delhi and 3\,350 nationwide
 \, whilst other sources estimate the number of deaths at about 8\,000–17
 \,000.\n\nProtest: India\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1984_anti-
 Sikh_riots\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.p
 ages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Protest
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1984_anti-Sikh_riots
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
