DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19850923
SUMMARY:Treaty signed: Plaza Accord
DESCRIPTION:The Plaza Accord was a joint agreement signed on September 22\,
  1985\, at the Plaza Hotel in New York City\, between France\, West German
 y\, Japan\, the United Kingdom\, and the United States\, to depreciate the
  U.S. dollar in relation to the French franc\, the German Deutsche Mark\, 
 the Japanese yen and the British pound sterling by intervening in currency
  markets.\n\nTreaty: International\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/
 Plaza_Accord\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi
 .pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Treaty
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plaza_Accord
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
