DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19860609
SUMMARY:1986 Austrian presidential election
DESCRIPTION:Presidential elections were held in Austria on 4 May 1986 with 
 a second round on 8 June 1986. Kurt Waldheim\, former Secretary-General of
  the United Nations\, endorsed by the Austrian People's Party (ÖVP) was e
 lected\, the first time the ÖVP had won a direct presidential election.\n
 \nElection: Austria\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1986_Austrian_p
 residential_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manag
 er (jdpi.pages.dev).
