SUMMARY:1987 Surinamese constitutional referendum
DESCRIPTION:A constitutional referendum was held in Suriname on 30 Septembe
 r 1987. Voters were asked to approve the country's new constitution. It pr
 ovided for a 51-seat unicameral National Assembly elected by proportional 
 representation and a President elected by the National Assembly. Over 96% 
 voted in favour\, with a turnout of 63%.\n\nReferendum: Suriname\nSource: 
 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1987_Surinamese_constitutional_referendum\nT
