SUMMARY:1987 Botswana electoral reform referendum
DESCRIPTION:A referendum on electoral reform was held in Botswana on 27 Oct
 ober 1987\, the first time a referendum had been held in the country. The 
 proposal involved the creation of the post of Supervisor of Elections\, wh
 ich would be appointed by the government. The referendum was passed with 7
 8.1% of voters in favour.\n\nReferendum: Botswana\nSource: https://en.wiki
 pedia.org/wiki/1987_Botswana_electoral_reform_referendum\nText: Wikipedia 
 (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via Vitruvian Manager (jdpi.pages.dev).
