SUMMARY:1989 Soviet Union legislative election (Soviet Union / Russia)
DESCRIPTION:Legislative elections were held in the Soviet Union on 26 March
  1989 to elect members of the Congress of People's Deputies\, with run-off
 s on 2\, 9 and 20 April and 14 and 23 May. They were the first partially f
 ree nationwide elections held in the Soviet Union\, and would be the last 
 national elections held in that country before its dissolution in 1991.\n\
