SUMMARY:Massacre of Tbilisi (Georgia)
DESCRIPTION:Massacre of Tbilisi refers to the events in Tbilisi\, Georgian 
 Soviet Socialist Republic\, on April 9\, 1989\, when a peaceful anti-Sovie
 t\, pro-independence and nationalist demonstration was violently dispersed
  by the Soviet Army\, resulting in the deaths of 21 Georgian civilians\, w
 ith hundreds more injured.\n\nProtest: Georgia\nSource: https://en.wikiped
