SUMMARY:Treaty signed: Convention on the Rights of the Child (United States
 )
DESCRIPTION:The United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child is an 
 international human rights treaty which sets out the civil\, political\, e
 conomic\, social\, health\, and cultural rights of children. The conventio
 n defines a child as any human being under the age of eighteen\, unless th
 e age of majority is attained earlier under national legislation.\n\nTreat
